          <ns0:quote>Cefeo</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>(Greek mythology) Husband of Cassiopeia, king of Eritrea, father of Andromeda. There may be two mythical kings by this name.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>Cefeo</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>Cefeus</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>(constellation) A circumpolar constellation of the northern sky, located between Draco and Cassiopeia and representing the king Cepheus from Greek myth. It contains the star Alderamin.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
