        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>desigualdad de Chebyshov</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>(statistics) The theorem that in any data sample with finite variance, the probability of any random variable X that lies k or more standard deviations away from the mean is no more than 1/k2, i.e. assuming mean μ and standard deviation σ, the probability is:</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
