        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>(neurology, genetic disorder) A genetic disorder caused by the presence of all or part of a third copy of chromosome 21 (a chromosomal excess), whereby the patients typically have a delay in cognitive ability and physical growth, as well as a small head and tilted eyelids. [from 1961.]</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
