        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>Of or relating to Finno-Ugric languages.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>First Lady</ns0:orth>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>n</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>primera dama</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>The wife of the chief executive of a nation; especially the wife of the President of a country; or a woman (e.g. a relative) who takes on similar public duties, as when the chief executive is unmarried.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>First Nation</ns0:orth>
        <ns0:pron>/ˌfɜɹs(t) ˈneɪʃən/</ns0:pron>
        <ns0:pron>/ˌfɜːs(t) ˈneɪʃn/</ns0:pron>
        <ns0:pron>/ˌfɜːs(t) ˈnæeʃ(ə)n/</ns0:pron>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>n</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>Nación Originaria en Canadá</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>Primera Nación</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>(Canada) A community of indigenous peoples of Canada (typically not including the Inuit or Metis), especially one officially recognized by the federal government. [from late 1970s]</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>First Vision</ns0:orth>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>pn</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>Primera Visión</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>(Mormonism) The appearance of God the Father and Jesus Christ to the fourteen-year-old Joseph Smith, Jr. in a wooded area (now called the Sacred Grove) near Palmyra, New York in the early spring of 1820.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>First World</ns0:orth>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>pn</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>primer mundo</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>(historical, politics) Those countries aligned with the West during the Cold War.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>(informal) Wealthy, developed nations.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>Fittipaldi</ns0:orth>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>pn</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>Fittipaldi</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>Flanderization</ns0:orth>
        <ns0:pron>/-ˌɹaɪ-/</ns0:pron>
        <ns0:pron>/ˌflændəɹəˈzeɪʃn̩/</ns0:pron>
        <ns0:pron>/ˌflændɚɹəˈzeɪʃ(ə)n/</ns0:pron>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>n</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>Flanderización</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>(uncountable) The progressive exaggeration of a single trait or set of traits of a fictional character until it overtakes all other characterization [from c. 2006]</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>Flanders</ns0:orth>
        <ns0:pron>/ˈflæn.dɚz/</ns0:pron>
        <ns0:pron>/ˈflɑːn.dəz/</ns0:pron>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>pn</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>Flandes</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>A historical county of Western Europe; in full, County of Flanders.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>A region of Belgium. Official name: Flemish Region.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>A community of Belgium. Official name: Flemish Community.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>Two provinces in Belgian Flanders, West Flanders and East Flanders.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>Ellipsis of French Flanders: a former province of France.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>Ellipsis of French Flanders: a region of France.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>Flaubertian</ns0:orth>
        <ns0:pron>/floʊˈbɝti.ən/</ns0:pron>
        <ns0:pron>/fləʊˈbɜːtɪən/</ns0:pron>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>adj</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>flaubertiano</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>Of or relating to Gustave Flaubert (1821–1880), influential French novelist in the style of literary realism.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>Fleming</ns0:orth>
        <ns0:pron>/ˈflɛmɪŋ/</ns0:pron>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>n</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>flamenco</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>flamenca</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>A native or inhabitant of Flanders in Belgium.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>Flemish</ns0:orth>
        <ns0:pron>/ˈflɛmɪʃ/</ns0:pron>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>adj</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>flamenco</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>Of or relating to Flanders, either as the historical county of Flanders (the current provinces of West Flanders and East Flanders in Belgium, Zeelandic Flanders in the Netherlands and French Flanders); or as the Dutch-speaking region of Belgium.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>Flemish</ns0:orth>
        <ns0:pron>/ˈflɛmɪʃ/</ns0:pron>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>pn</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>flamenco</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>Standard Dutch as it is spoken in Flanders.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>Flood</ns0:orth>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>pn</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>diluvio universal</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>(biblical) The flood referred to in the Book of Genesis in the Hebrew Bible.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>Flora</ns0:orth>
        <ns0:pron>/ˈflɔːɹə/</ns0:pron>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>pn</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>Flora</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>(Roman god) the goddess of flowers, nature and spring; she is also the wife of Favonius and the mother of Karpos. She is the Roman counterpart of Chloris.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>A en given name.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>Floreana</ns0:orth>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>pn</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>Floreana</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>isla</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>Florence</ns0:orth>
        <ns0:pron>/ˈfloɹəns/</ns0:pron>
        <ns0:pron>/ˈflɑɹɪns/</ns0:pron>
        <ns0:pron>/ˈflɒɹəns/</ns0:pron>
        <ns0:pron>/ˈflɒɹəns/&lt;a:RP&gt;</ns0:pron>
        <ns0:pron>/ˈflɔɹəns/</ns0:pron>
        <ns0:pron>[ˈflɔ̟ɹəns]</ns0:pron>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>pn</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>Florencia</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>A city and comune, the capital of the Metropolitan City of Florence and the region of Tuscany, Italy.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>A metropolitan city of Tuscany, established in 2015; in full, the Metropolitan City of Florence.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>A en given name.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>(obsolete) A en given name.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>Florentine</ns0:orth>
        <ns0:pron>/ˈflɒɹəntaɪn/</ns0:pron>
        <ns0:pron>/ˈflɔɹəntin/</ns0:pron>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>adj</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>florentino</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>Of, from or relating to the city of Florence, Tuscany, Italy.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>Florentine</ns0:orth>
        <ns0:pron>/ˈflɒɹəntaɪn/</ns0:pron>
        <ns0:pron>/ˈflɔɹəntin/</ns0:pron>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>n</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>florentino</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>florentina</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>A native or inhabitant of the city of Florence, Tuscany, Italy.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>Florida</ns0:orth>
        <ns0:pron>/ˈfloɹ.də/</ns0:pron>
        <ns0:pron>/ˈfloɹ.ə.də/</ns0:pron>
        <ns0:pron>/ˈfloɹ.ɪ.də/</ns0:pron>
        <ns0:pron>/ˈflɑɹ.ɪ.də/</ns0:pron>
        <ns0:pron>/ˈflɒɹ.ə.də/</ns0:pron>
        <ns0:pron>/ˈflɒɹ.ɪ.də/</ns0:pron>
        <ns0:pron>/ˈflɔ.ɹə.də/</ns0:pron>
        <ns0:pron>/ˈflɔ.ɹɪ.də/</ns0:pron>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>pn</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>Florida</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>A state of the United States. Capital: Tallahassee. Largest city: Jacksonville.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>Florida Keys</ns0:orth>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>pn</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>cayos de Florida</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>A coral cay archipelago located off the southern coast of Florida.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>Florida panther</ns0:orth>
        <ns0:pron>/ˈflɑɹ.ɪ.də ˈpæn.θɚ/</ns0:pron>
        <ns0:pron>/ˈflɒɹ.ə.də ˈpæn.θə/</ns0:pron>
        <ns0:pron>/ˈflɒɹ.ɪ.də ˈpæn.θə/</ns0:pron>
        <ns0:pron>/ˈflɔɹ.də ˈpæn.θɚ/</ns0:pron>
        <ns0:pron>/ˈflɔɹ.ə.də ˈpæn.θɚ/</ns0:pron>
        <ns0:pron>/ˈflɔɹ.ɪ.də ˈpæn.θɚ/</ns0:pron>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>n</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>pantera de Florida</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>puma norteamericano</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>Puma concolor cougar, an endangered cougar that lives in forests and swamps of southern Florida in the United States.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>Floridian</ns0:orth>
        <ns0:pron>/flɔˈɹɪdi.ən/</ns0:pron>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>n</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>floridense</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>floridano</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>A native or resident of the state of Florida in the United States of America.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>Florina</ns0:orth>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>pn</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>Flórina</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>A city in northern Greece near the border with the former Yugoslav Republic of Macedonia / Republic of North Macedonia.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>Floréal</ns0:orth>
        <ns0:pron>/ˈflɔːɹɪ.əl/</ns0:pron>
        <ns0:pron>/ˌflɔɹeɪˈɑl/</ns0:pron>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>pn</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>floreal</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>(historical) The eighth month of the French Republican Calendar, from April 20 or 21 to May 19 or 20.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>Flying Dutchman</ns0:orth>
        <ns0:pron>/ˌflaɪ.ɪŋ ˈdʌtʃ.mən/</ns0:pron>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>pn</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>Holandés Errante</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>Holandés Volador</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>(nautical, _, folklore) A mythical Dutch-flagged ghost clipper that is very fast sailing, and never makes it to port, seen on the high seas, where be hailed, occupants request information on persons long dead, or leave messages for said people. In European naval folklore, it was considered to portend bad luck.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>Flying Fortress</ns0:orth>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>pn</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>Fortaleza Volante</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>(informal) The Boeing B-17, a United States WWII heavy bomber, based upon a reputation for toughness and reliability, as well as its relatively heavy defensive armament at the expense of bombload.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>Flying Spaghetti Monster</ns0:orth>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>pn</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>Monstruo de Espagueti Volador</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>(humorous) A deity consisting of spaghetti and meatballs, the creator of the universe according to the religion of Pastafarianism.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>Fomalhaut</ns0:orth>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>pn</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>Fomalhaut</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>(star) The brightest star in the constellation Piscis Austrinus and one of the brightest stars in the night sky; Alpha (α) Piscis Austrini.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
