        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>(zodiac constellations) A constellation of the zodiac traditionally taken to represent the pair of twins Castor and Pollux in Greek mythology. It contains the stars Castor, Pollux, and Alhena.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>(astrology) The zodiac sign for the twins, ruled by Mercury and covering May 22 – June 21 (tropical astrology) or June 16 – July 15 (sidereal astrology).</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
