      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>ley de Hooke</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>(physics) the principle that the stress applied to a solid is directly proportional to the strain produced. This law describes the behavior of springs and solids stressed within their elastic limit.</ns0:def>
