      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>pn</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>lucero</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>lucífero</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>(literary) The planet Venus as the daystar (the morning star).</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>Lucifer</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>(biblical) The King of Babylon who was compared to the planet Venus in first the Wycliffe version then the King James Version of Isaiah 14:12; it is unclear whether this verse refers to a specific king or to a representation of the entire line of kings of Babylon.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
