          <ns0:quote>Melusina</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>(mythology) A figure of European folklore and mythology (mostly Celtic), a female spirit of fresh water in a sacred spring or river, usually depicted as a serpent or fish from the waist down, and sometimes with wings.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
