      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>Serpens</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>(constellation) A large summer constellation of the northern sky said to resemble a snake. It is the only constellation consisting of two parts (Serpens Caput and Serpens Cauda) separated by the constellation Ophiuchus, representing the snake handler Asclepius.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
