        <ns0:orth>are you OK</ns0:orth>
        <ns0:pron>/ɑɹ juː oʊˈkeɪ/</ns0:pron>
        <ns0:pron>/ɑː juː əʊˈkeɪ/</ns0:pron>
        <ns0:pron>[ɑ̟ɹ ju̟ː oʊˈkʰeɪ]</ns0:pron>
        <ns0:pron>[ɑ̟ː ju̟ː əʊˈkʰeɪ]</ns0:pron>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>phraseologicalUnit</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>¿está bien?</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>¿estás bien?</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>Asking if the listener is OK (e.g. not hurt).</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>are you allergic to any medications</ns0:orth>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>phraseologicalUnit</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>¿eres alérgica a algún medicamento?</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>¿eres alérgico a algún medicamento?</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>¿es usted alérgica a algún medicamento?</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>¿es usted alérgico a algún medicamento?</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>Asked mostly by doctors and nurses to ascertain whether certain medications should not be given to patients.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>are you doing anything tomorrow</ns0:orth>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>phraseologicalUnit</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>¿qué va a hacer mañana?</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>¿qué vas a hacer mañana?</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>Asks if someone is busy tomorrow, possibly to invite them to do something if they are available. ("Tomorrow" can be replaced by other dates, such as "are you doing anything on the weekend", etc.)</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>are you feeling better</ns0:orth>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>phraseologicalUnit</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>estás mejor</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>Asked to find out whether someone has recovered to some degree from past illness or unwellness.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>are you married</ns0:orth>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>phraseologicalUnit</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>¿está casada?</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>¿está casado?</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>¿estás casada?</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>¿estás casado?</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>Used to ask whether the interlocutor does or doesn't have a spouse.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>are you religious</ns0:orth>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>phraseologicalUnit</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>¿eres religiosa?</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>¿eres religioso?</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>¿es usted religiosa?</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>¿es usted religioso?</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>A request for information about the listener's (or listeners') religious beliefs.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>are you single</ns0:orth>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>phraseologicalUnit</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>¿está soltera?</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>¿está soltero?</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>¿estás soltera?</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>¿estás soltero?</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>Used to ask whether the interlocutor does or doesn't have a (romantic) partner.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>are you taking any medications</ns0:orth>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>phraseologicalUnit</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>¿está usted tomando algún medicamento?</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>¿estás tomando algún medicamento?</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>Asked mostly by doctors and nurses to ascertain whether certain drugs should not be given to patients, as they may interact adversely with other medications.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>area</ns0:orth>
        <ns0:pron>/ˈerɪjɑ/</ns0:pron>
        <ns0:pron>/ˈɛə.ɹɪ.ə/</ns0:pron>
        <ns0:pron>/ˈɛɹ.i.ə/</ns0:pron>
        <ns0:pron>[ˈɛː.ɹɪ.ə]</ns0:pron>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>n</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>área</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>superficie</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>(mathematics) A measure of the extent of a surface; it is measured in square units.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>área</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>región</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>A particular geographic region.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>área</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>Any particular extent of surface, especially an empty or unused extent.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>patio inglés</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>(British) An open space, below ground level, giving access to the basement of a house, and typically separated from the pavement by railings. [from 18th c.]</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>area code</ns0:orth>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>n</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>prefijo</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>indicativo</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>(US, Australia, Philippines) A prefix appended to a telephone number indicating the geographical area.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>areal</ns0:orth>
        <ns0:pron>/ˈɛəɹiəl/</ns0:pron>
        <ns0:pron>/ˈɛəɹɪəl/</ns0:pron>
        <ns0:pron>/ˈɛɹiəl/</ns0:pron>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>adj</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>areal</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>Of or pertaining to an area.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>areca</ns0:orth>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>n</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>areca</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>Any member of the genus Areca of about fifty species of single-stemmed palms in the family Arecaceae, found in humid tropical forests.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>arena</ns0:orth>
        <ns0:pron>/əˈɹiːnə/</ns0:pron>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>n</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>arena</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>ruedo</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>redondel</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>albero</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>estadio</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>liza</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>An enclosed area, often outdoor, for the presentation of sporting events (sports arena) or other spectacular events; earthen area, often oval, specifically for rodeos (North America) or circular area for bullfights (especially Hispanic America).</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>arena</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>The building housing such an area; specifically, a very large, often round building, often topped with a dome, designated for indoor sporting or other major events, such as concerts.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>arene</ns0:orth>
        <ns0:pron>/ˈæɹiːn/</ns0:pron>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>n</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>areno</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>(organic chemistry) Any monocyclic or polycyclic aromatic hydrocarbon.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>arenicolous</ns0:orth>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>adj</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>arenícola</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>(biology) Living or burrowing in sand.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>areocentric</ns0:orth>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>adj</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>areocéntrico</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>(astronomy) Having the planet Mars at the center.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>areola</ns0:orth>
        <ns0:pron>/əˈɹi.ə.lə/</ns0:pron>
        <ns0:pron>/ˌæ.ɹiˈəʊ.lə/</ns0:pron>
        <ns0:pron>/ˌæɹ.iˈoʊ.lə/</ns0:pron>
        <ns0:pron>/ˌɛɹ.iˈoʊ.lə/</ns0:pron>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>n</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>areola</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>(anatomy) The circular, darkly pigmented area surrounding a nipple; the areola mammae.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>areolar</ns0:orth>
        <ns0:pron>/əˈɹiːə.lə(ɹ)/</ns0:pron>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>adj</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>areolar</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>(anatomy) Of or relating to areolae.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>(botany) Of or relating to areoles.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>areometer</ns0:orth>
        <ns0:pron>/ɛːriːˈɒmɪtə/</ns0:pron>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>n</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>areómetro</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>Any device used to measure the specific gravity of liquids or the density of solids.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>aretology</ns0:orth>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>n</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>aretalogía</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>(philosophy) The part of moral philosophy that deals with virtue, its nature, and how to attain it.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>arf</ns0:orth>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>interjection</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>guau</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>argali</ns0:orth>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>n</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>argalí</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>Ovis ammon, the largest wild sheep, which roams the highlands of Central Asia.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>argan</ns0:orth>
        <ns0:pron>/ˈɑː(ɹ)ɡən/</ns0:pron>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>n</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>argán</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>erguén</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>Fruit of this tree.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>argent</ns0:orth>
        <ns0:pron>/ˈɑɹd͡ʒənt/</ns0:pron>
        <ns0:pron>/ˈɑːdʒənt/</ns0:pron>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>adj</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>argénteo</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>Of silver or silver-coloured.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>plata</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>blanco</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>(tincture) : of white or silver tincture on a coat of arms.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>argent</ns0:orth>
        <ns0:pron>/ˈɑɹd͡ʒənt/</ns0:pron>
        <ns0:pron>/ˈɑːdʒənt/</ns0:pron>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>n</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>plata</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>(tincture) The white or silver tincture on a coat of arms.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>argentiferous</ns0:orth>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>adj</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>argentífero</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>(geology) Containing or producing silver.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>argentine</ns0:orth>
        <ns0:pron>/ˈɑː(ɹ).d͡ʒənˌtaɪn/</ns0:pron>
        <ns0:pron>/ˈɑː(ɹ).d͡ʒənˌtiːn/</ns0:pron>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>n</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>argentina</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>pez plata</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>Any osmeriform fish of the genus Argentina, especially a European argentine (Argentina sphyraena).</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>argentite</ns0:orth>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>n</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>argentita</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>argirita</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>(mineral) Silver sulfide, (Ag2S), a primary ore of silver, in cubic or hexoctahedral crystals.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>argillaceous</ns0:orth>
        <ns0:pron>/ɑːd͡ʒɪlˈeɪʃəs/</ns0:pron>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>adj</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>arcilloso</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>(chiefly, geology) Pertaining to clay; made of, containing, or resembling clay; clayey.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>arginine</ns0:orth>
        <ns0:pron>/ˈɑɹɡɪniːn/</ns0:pron>
        <ns0:pron>/ˈɑːdʒɪniːn/</ns0:pron>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>n</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>arginina</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>An amino acid found in animal foods that plays an important role in several physiological processes.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>argon</ns0:orth>
        <ns0:pron>/ˈɑːɹɡɒn/</ns0:pron>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>n</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>argón</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>argon</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>The chemical element (symbol Ar) with an atomic number of 18. The third most abundant gas in the Earth's atmosphere, it is a colourless, odourless, inert noble gas.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>argot</ns0:orth>
        <ns0:pron>/ˈɑɹɡoʊ/</ns0:pron>
        <ns0:pron>/ˈɑɹɡət/</ns0:pron>
        <ns0:pron>/ˈɑːɡəʊ/</ns0:pron>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>n</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>argot</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>A secret language or conventional slang peculiar to thieves, tramps and vagabonds.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>The specialized informal vocabulary and terminology used between people with special skill in a field, such as between doctors, mathematicians or hackers.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>argotic</ns0:orth>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>adj</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>argótico</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>(rare, linguistics) Of or belonging to argot.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>arguable</ns0:orth>
        <ns0:pron>/ˈɑɹɡjuəbl/</ns0:pron>
        <ns0:pron>/ˈɑːɡjuəbl/</ns0:pron>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>adj</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>discutible</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>(colloquial) Open to doubt, argument or debate.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>arguably</ns0:orth>
        <ns0:pron>/ˈɑɹɡjuəbli/</ns0:pron>
        <ns0:pron>/ˈɑːɡjuəbli/</ns0:pron>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>adv</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>argüiblemente</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>As can be supported or proven by sound logical deduction, evidence, and precedent, but without absolute certainty.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>argue</ns0:orth>
        <ns0:pron>/ˈɑɹ.ɡju/</ns0:pron>
        <ns0:pron>/ˈɑː.ɡjuː/</ns0:pron>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>v</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>argumentar</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>debatir</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>(intransitive) To debate, disagree, or discuss opposing or differing viewpoints; to controvert; to wrangle.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>discutir</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>altercar</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>disputar</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>polemizar</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>porfiar</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>reñir</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>(intransitive) To have an argument, a quarrel.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>argumentar</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>(transitive) To present (a viewpoint or an argument therefor).</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>argument</ns0:orth>
        <ns0:pron>/-ɡju-/</ns0:pron>
        <ns0:pron>/-ɡjə-/</ns0:pron>
        <ns0:pron>/ˈɑɹɡjʊmənt/</ns0:pron>
        <ns0:pron>/ˈɑːɡjʊmənt/</ns0:pron>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>n</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>discusión</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>pelea</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>riña</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>altercación</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>altercado</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>argüende</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
      </ns0:sense>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>argumento</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>(countable, also, figuratively) A fact or statement used to support a proposition; a reason.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>A value, or a reference to a value, passed to a function.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>The subject matter of an artistic representation, discourse, or writing; a theme or topic.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>argumentación</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>(countable) A process of reasoning; argumentation.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>argumento</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>variable dependiente</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>The independent variable of a function.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>argumentative</ns0:orth>
        <ns0:pron>/ˌɑɹɡjəˈmɛn(t)ətɪv/</ns0:pron>
        <ns0:pron>/ˌɑːɡjʊmɛnˈteɪtɪv/</ns0:pron>
        <ns0:pron>/ˌɑːɡjʊˈmɛntətɪv/</ns0:pron>
        <ns0:pron>[-ɾɪv]</ns0:pron>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>adj</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>arguyente</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>argüidor</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>argüitivo</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>beligerante</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>contencioso</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>discutidor</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>Prone to argue or dispute.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>argyle</ns0:orth>
        <ns0:pron>/ˈɑɹ.ɡaɪl/</ns0:pron>
        <ns0:pron>/ˈɑː.ɡaɪl/</ns0:pron>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>n</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>diseño de rombos</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>a sock having this pattern</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>aria</ns0:orth>
        <ns0:pron>/ˈɑː.ɹi.ə/</ns0:pron>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>n</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>aria</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>(music) A musical piece written typically for a solo voice with orchestral accompaniment in an opera or cantata.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>arid</ns0:orth>
        <ns0:pron>/ˈæɹ.ɪd/</ns0:pron>
        <ns0:pron>/ˈɛɚ.ɪd/</ns0:pron>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>adj</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>árido</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>Very dry.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>aridity</ns0:orth>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>n</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>aridez</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>A long-term lack of rainfall or moisture.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>arigato</ns0:orth>
        <ns0:pron>/-ɡæ-/</ns0:pron>
        <ns0:pron>/-ɹɪ-/</ns0:pron>
        <ns0:pron>/æ-/</ns0:pron>
        <ns0:pron>/ˌɑːɹiˈɡɑːtoʊ/</ns0:pron>
        <ns0:pron>/ˌɑːɹiˈɡɑːtəʊ/</ns0:pron>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>interjection</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>arigató</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>(colloquial) Thank you (used in the context of, or to evoke, Japanese culture).</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>aril</ns0:orth>
        <ns0:pron>/ˈærɪl/</ns0:pron>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>n</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>arilo</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>(botany) A tissue surrounding the seed in certain fruits such as pomegranates.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>arise</ns0:orth>
        <ns0:pron>/əˈɹaɪz/</ns0:pron>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>v</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>levantarse</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>surgir</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>(intransitive) To come up from one's bed or place of repose; to get up.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>nacer</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>surgir</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>aparecer</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>dimanar</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>provenir</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>(intransitive) To spring up; to come into action, being, or notice; to become operative, sensible, or visible; to begin to act a part; to present itself.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>arista</ns0:orth>
        <ns0:pron>/əˈɹɪstə/</ns0:pron>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>n</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>arista</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>raspa</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>(biology) One of the fibrils found on grains or fishes.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>aristocracy</ns0:orth>
        <ns0:pron>/ˌæ.ɹɪˈstɒk.ɹə.si/</ns0:pron>
        <ns0:pron>/ˌɛɹ.ɪˈstɑk.ɹə.si/</ns0:pron>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>n</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>aristocracia</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>The nobility, or the hereditary ruling class.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>Government by such a class, or a state with such a government.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>A class of people considered (not normally universally) superior to others.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>aristocrat</ns0:orth>
        <ns0:pron>/əˈɹɪstəˌkɹæt/</ns0:pron>
        <ns0:pron>/ˈæɹɪstəˌkɹæt/</ns0:pron>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>n</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>aristócrata</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>One of the aristocracy, nobility, or people of rank in a community; one of a ruling class; a noble (originally in Revolutionary France).</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>aristocratic</ns0:orth>
        <ns0:pron>/ˌæɹɪstəˈkɹætɪk/</ns0:pron>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>adj</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>aristocrático</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>Of, pertaining to, or favouring, an aristocracy</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>Similar to the aristocracy; characteristic of, the aristocracy.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>aristocratically</ns0:orth>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>adv</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>aristocráticamente</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>in an aristocratic manner</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>arithmancy</ns0:orth>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>n</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>aritmancia</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>aritmomancia</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>Divination using numbers that are the equivalent of letters of a name</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>arithmetic</ns0:orth>
        <ns0:pron>/æɹɪθˈmɛtɪk/</ns0:pron>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>adj</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>aritmético</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>arismético</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>(mathematics) Of, relating to, or using arithmetic; arithmetical.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>arithmetic</ns0:orth>
        <ns0:pron>/əˈɹɪθmətɪk/</ns0:pron>
        <ns0:pron>/ˌæɹɪθˈmɛtɪk/</ns0:pron>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>n</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>aritmética</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>arismética</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>The mathematics of numbers (integers, rational numbers, real numbers, or complex numbers) under the operations of addition, subtraction, multiplication, and division.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>arithmetic mean</ns0:orth>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>n</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>media aritmética</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>(statistics, probability) The measure of central tendency of a set of values computed by dividing the sum of the values by their number.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>arithmetic progression</ns0:orth>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>n</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>progresión aritmética</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>(analysis) A sequence in which each term except the first is obtained from the previous by adding a constant value, known as the common difference of the arithmetic progression.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>arithmetically</ns0:orth>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>adv</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>aritméticamente</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>(of the nature of increases or decreases) In a way characterized by addition (of increments) rather than multiplication (by factors) or exponentiation (by exponents): by an arithmetic progression.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>In terms of arithmetic.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>arithmomania</ns0:orth>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>n</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>aritmomanía</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>an obsessive-compulsive disorder in which the subject feels the need to count things</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>arity</ns0:orth>
        <ns0:pron>/ˈeəɹɪti/</ns0:pron>
        <ns0:pron>/ˈæɹɪti/</ns0:pron>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>n</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>aridad</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>(logic, mathematics, computer science) The number of arguments or operands a function or operation takes. For a relation, the number of domains in the corresponding Cartesian product.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>ark</ns0:orth>
        <ns0:pron>/ɑɹk/</ns0:pron>
        <ns0:pron>/ɑːk/</ns0:pron>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>n</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>arca</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>(Judaism, Christianity, Islam) Noah's ark: the ship built by Noah to save his family and a collection of animals from the deluge.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>(Judaism) A decorated cabinet at the front of a synagogue, in which Torah scrolls are kept.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>arkose</ns0:orth>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>n</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>arcosa</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>(geology) An arenite sandstone consisting of at least 25% feldspar grains.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>arm</ns0:orth>
        <ns0:pron>/ɐːm/</ns0:pron>
        <ns0:pron>/ɑɹm/</ns0:pron>
        <ns0:pron>/ɑːm/</ns0:pron>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>n</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>brazo</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>(anatomy) The portion of the upper human appendage, from the shoulder to the wrist and sometimes including the hand.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>A long, narrow, more or less rigid part of an object extending from the main part or centre of the object, such as the armrest of an armchair, a crane, a pair of spectacles or a pair of compasses.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>arma</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>(usually used in the plural) A weapon.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>arm</ns0:orth>
        <ns0:pron>/ɐːm/</ns0:pron>
        <ns0:pron>/ɑɹm/</ns0:pron>
        <ns0:pron>/ɑːm/</ns0:pron>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>v</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>armar</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>(transitive) To supply with armour or (later especially) weapons.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>(transitive, figurative) To supply with the equipment, knowledge, authority, or other tools needed for a particular task; to furnish with capability; to equip.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>(intransitive) To take up weapons; to arm oneself.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>arm to the teeth</ns0:orth>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>v</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>armar hasta los dientes</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>(idiomatic, informal, transitive, intransitive) To equip thoroughly with weapons.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>arm wrestling</ns0:orth>
        <ns0:pron>/ˈɑɹm ˌɹɛs.lɪŋ/</ns0:pron>
        <ns0:pron>/ˈɑːm ˌɹɛs.lɪŋ/</ns0:pron>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>n</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>pulso</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>pulseada</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>fuercitas</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>A strength sport with two participants, in which each participant grips the other's hand and tries to pin the other's arm onto a surface.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>arm-wrestle</ns0:orth>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>v</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>echar un pulso</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>echar unas fuercitas</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>pulsear</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>(ambitransitive) To compete in an arm-wrestle (with).</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>arm-wrestler</ns0:orth>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>n</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>pulseador</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>pulseadora</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>Someone who arm-wrestles.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>armada</ns0:orth>
        <ns0:pron>/ɑɹˈmɑdə/</ns0:pron>
        <ns0:pron>/ɑːˈmɑːdə/</ns0:pron>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>n</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>armada</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>flota</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>A fleet of warships, especially with reference to the Spanish Armada.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>armadillo</ns0:orth>
        <ns0:pron>/ɑɹməˈdɪloʊ/</ns0:pron>
        <ns0:pron>/ɑːməˈdɪləʊ/</ns0:pron>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>n</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>armadillo</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>armado</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>cachicamo</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>carachupa</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>cusuco</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>gurre</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>Any of the burrowing mammals covered with bony, jointed, protective plates, families Dasypodidae and Chlamyphoridae in the order Cingulata, found in the Americas, especially in South America.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>armageddon</ns0:orth>
        <ns0:pron>/-ˈɡɛ.dən/</ns0:pron>
        <ns0:pron>/ɑː(ɹ).məˈɡɛd.ʔn/</ns0:pron>
        <ns0:pron>/ˌɑɹ.məˈɡɛ.dn̩/</ns0:pron>
        <ns0:pron>/ˌɑː(ɹ).məˈɡɛ.dn̩/</ns0:pron>
        <ns0:pron>[ˌɑɹ.məˈɡɛɾ.ʔn]</ns0:pron>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>n</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>armagedón</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>The scene of a decisive conflict on a great scale.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>armalcolite</ns0:orth>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>n</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>armalcolita</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>(mineral) An orthorhombic mineral first discovered on the Moon.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>armament</ns0:orth>
        <ns0:pron>/ˈɑː(ɹ)məmənt/</ns0:pron>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>n</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>armamento</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>(military, naval) All the cannon and small arms collectively, with their equipments, belonging to a ship or a fortification.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>Any equipment for resistance.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>The process of building up military capacity.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>armature</ns0:orth>
        <ns0:pron>/ˈɑɹ.mə.tjʊɚ/</ns0:pron>
        <ns0:pron>/ˈɑɹ.mə.t͡ʃɚ/</ns0:pron>
        <ns0:pron>/ˈɑɹ.mə.t͡ʃʊɚ/</ns0:pron>
        <ns0:pron>/ˈɑː.mə.tjə/</ns0:pron>
        <ns0:pron>/ˈɑː.mə.tjʊə/</ns0:pron>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>n</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>inducido</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>The rotating part of an electric motor or dynamo, which mostly consists of coils of wire (the winding) around a metal core.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>armband</ns0:orth>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>n</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>brazalete</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>brazal</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>(sports) A band worn around the arm of the captain of a team.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>flotador</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>manguito</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>(swimming) One of a pair of inflatable plastic bands, normally worn on the upper arms, to help the wearer (often a child) float in water and learn to swim.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>armbrace</ns0:orth>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>n</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>cabestrillo</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>charpa</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>armchair</ns0:orth>
        <ns0:pron>/ˈɑɹmt͡ʃɛɚ/</ns0:pron>
        <ns0:pron>/ˈɑː(ɹ)mtʃɛə(ɹ)/</ns0:pron>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>adj</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>de salón</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>de sillón</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>(figuratively) Remote from actual involvement, including a person retired from previously active involvement.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>(figuratively, derogatory) Unqualified or uninformed but yet giving advice, especially on technical issues, such as law, architecture, medicine, military theory, or sports; relating to such advice.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>armchair</ns0:orth>
        <ns0:pron>/ˈɑɹmt͡ʃɛɚ/</ns0:pron>
        <ns0:pron>/ˈɑː(ɹ)mtʃɛə(ɹ)/</ns0:pron>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>n</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>sillón</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>butaca</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>poltrona</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>silla poltrona</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>A chair with supports for the arms or elbows.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>armed</ns0:orth>
        <ns0:pron>/ɑɹmd/</ns0:pron>
        <ns0:pron>/ɑːmd/</ns0:pron>
        <ns0:pron>/ˈɑːɹmɪd/</ns0:pron>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>adj</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>armado [con]</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>armífero</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>provisto [de]</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>armado</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>(of a person, specifically) Equipped with a gun.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>(sometimes, in combination) Equipped, especially with a weapon.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>con brazo</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>con brazos</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>(chiefly, in combination) Having an arm or arms, often of a specified number or type.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>armed conflict</ns0:orth>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>n</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>conflito armado</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>(international law, military) A contested incompatibility that entails the use of armed force between two parties including a territory, the government of a state, or both.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>armed forces</ns0:orth>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>n</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>fuerzas armadas</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>The military forces of a nation, such as the army, navy, air force, marines, and sometimes, coastguard or border guard, which are tasked with the defence of the nation and its citizens, if necessary through use of deadly force.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>armed robbery</ns0:orth>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>n</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>robo a mano armada</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>(legal) A theft where the thieves are armed with weapons.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>armful</ns0:orth>
        <ns0:pron>/ˈɑɹmˌfl̩/</ns0:pron>
        <ns0:pron>/ˈɑːmfl̩/</ns0:pron>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>n</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>brazado</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>brazada</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>The amount an arm or arms can hold.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>armhole</ns0:orth>
        <ns0:pron>/ˈɑɹmˌhoʊl/</ns0:pron>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>n</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>sisa</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>sobaquera</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>(fashion) A hole for an arm in a piece of clothing.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>armiger</ns0:orth>
        <ns0:pron>/ˈɑːmɪdʒə/</ns0:pron>
        <ns0:pron>/ˈɑːɹmɪd͡ʒɚ/</ns0:pron>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>n</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>armígero</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>An esquire, originally carrying the armour of a knight; (hence, later) a man of the gentry ranking below a knight. [from 16th c.]</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>armigerous</ns0:orth>
        <ns0:pron>/ɑɹˈmɪ.d͡ʒɚ.əs/</ns0:pron>
        <ns0:pron>/ɑːˈmɪ.dʒə.ɹəs/</ns0:pron>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>adj</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>blasonado</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>hidalgo</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>Entitled to bear a coat of arms.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>armill</ns0:orth>
        <ns0:pron>/ˈɑɹməl/</ns0:pron>
        <ns0:pron>/ˈɑɹmɪl/</ns0:pron>
        <ns0:pron>/ˈɑːməl/</ns0:pron>
        <ns0:pron>/ˈɑːmɪl/</ns0:pron>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>n</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>armilla</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>(historical, astronomy) An ancient astronomical instrument, having either one ring placed in the plane of the equator for determining the time of the equinoxes (an equinoctial armil) or two or more rings, one in the plane of the meridian, for observing the solstices (a solstitial armil).</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>armillary</ns0:orth>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>adj</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>armilar</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>Resembling a bracelet or armilla; consisting of rings or circles.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>armillary sphere</ns0:orth>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>n</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>esfera armilar</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>An instrument consisting of graduated metal circles used to represent the motions of celestial bodies around the earth.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>armistice</ns0:orth>
        <ns0:pron>/-məstəs/</ns0:pron>
        <ns0:pron>/ˈɑɹmɪstɪs/</ns0:pron>
        <ns0:pron>/ˈɑːmɪstɪs/</ns0:pron>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>n</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>armisticio</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>(countable, military) A formal agreement, especially between nations, to end combat.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>armless</ns0:orth>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>adj</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>coto duplado</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>duplo cuto</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>sin brazos</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>Having no arms.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>armlet</ns0:orth>
        <ns0:pron>/ˈɑɹmlət/</ns0:pron>
        <ns0:pron>/ˈɑːmlət/</ns0:pron>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>n</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>carcax</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>A band worn on the arm for ornamental or identification purposes.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>armor</ns0:orth>
        <ns0:pron>/ˈɑː.mə/</ns0:pron>
        <ns0:pron>/ˈɑːɹ.mɚ/</ns0:pron>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>n</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>armadura</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>blindaje</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>(uncountable) A protective layer over a body, vehicle, or other object intended to deflect or diffuse damaging forces.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>coraza</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>(uncountable) A natural form of this kind of protection on an animal's body.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>blindado</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>(countable) A tank, or other heavy mobile assault vehicle.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>armored</ns0:orth>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>adj</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>acorazado</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>blindado</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>Clad or equipped with arms or armor.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>armored personnel carrier</ns0:orth>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>n</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>tanqueta</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>transporte blindado de personal / plantel</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>An armored vehicle for carrying infantry soldiers in combat.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>armorer</ns0:orth>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>n</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>armero</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>A manufacturer of weapons, especially of guns.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>armoured</ns0:orth>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>adj</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>blindado</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>Possessing, wearing, or fitted out with armour.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>armoured car</ns0:orth>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>n</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>carro blindado</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>coche blindado</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>vehículo blindado</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>An automobile equipped with armour to protect important passengers.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>blindado</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>carro blindado</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>vehículo blindado</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>(military) A small wheeled armoured fighting vehicle.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>armoured train</ns0:orth>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>n</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>tren blindado</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>a railway train protected with armour</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>armoured truck</ns0:orth>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>n</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>camión blindado</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>furgón blindado</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>vehículo blindado</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>A truck used to transfer valuables between locations, which possesses armour against light firearms.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>armoury</ns0:orth>
        <ns0:pron>/ˈɑɹməɹi/</ns0:pron>
        <ns0:pron>/ˈɑːməɹi/</ns0:pron>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>n</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>armería</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>A place where arms are kept, an arsenal.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>armpit</ns0:orth>
        <ns0:pron>/ˈɑɹmˌpɪt/</ns0:pron>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>n</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>axila</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>sobaco</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>The cavity beneath the junction of the arm and shoulder.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>armrest</ns0:orth>
        <ns0:pron>/ˈɑɹmˌɹɛst/</ns0:pron>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>n</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>apoyabrazos</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>reposabrazos</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>Part of the seat of a chair that is designed to support the arm.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>arms race</ns0:orth>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>n</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>carrera armamentista</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>carrera de armamentos</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>A competition for military supremacy between two powers, especially for the most weapons and the best military technology.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>arms-bearer</ns0:orth>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>n</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>armiguero</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>One who carries weapons for another.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>army</ns0:orth>
        <ns0:pron>/ˈɐː.mi(ː)/</ns0:pron>
        <ns0:pron>/ˈɑɹ.mi/</ns0:pron>
        <ns0:pron>/ˈɑː.miː/</ns0:pron>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>n</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>ejército</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>The governmental agency in charge of a state's army.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>(figuratively) A large group of people working toward the same purpose.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>(figuratively) A large group of social animals working toward the same purpose.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>ejército</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>multitud</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>(figuratively) Any multitude.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>army ant</ns0:orth>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>n</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>hormiga guerrera</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>hormiga legionaria</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>marabunta</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>A tropical nomadic ant, principally in the subfamilies Dorylinae and Leptanillinae, that preys on other insects.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>arnica</ns0:orth>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>n</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>árnica</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>Any of several plants, of the genus Arnica, considered to have medicinal properties, especially Arnica montana.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>aroma</ns0:orth>
        <ns0:pron>/əˈɹoʊmə/</ns0:pron>
        <ns0:pron>/əˈɹəʊmə/</ns0:pron>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>n</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>aroma</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>A smell; especially a pleasant spicy or fragrant one.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
