          <ns0:quote>tahalí</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>télamo</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>A broad belt, originally of leather and often richly ornamented, worn diagonally from shoulder to hip (across the breast and under the opposite arm), which was formerly used to hold a sword, a bugle, etc., and is now chiefly worn for ceremonial purposes; also (loosely) , any belt. [from 14th c.]</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>bale</ns0:orth>
