          <ns0:quote>pulsación</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>A pulsation or throb.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>pulsaciones (por minuto)</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>(music) A pulse on the beat level, the metric level at which pulses are heard as the basic unit. Thus a beat is the basic time unit of a piece.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>ritmo</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>A rhythm.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>jurisdicción</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>The route patrolled by a police officer or a guard.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>sector</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>ámbito</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>(by extension) An area of a person's responsibility, especially</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>sector</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>ámbito</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>área</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>(journalism) The primary focus of a reporter's stories (such as police/courts, education, city government, business etc.).</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>batida</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>(hunting) The act of scouring, or ranging over, a tract of land to rouse or drive out game; also, those so engaged, collectively.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>beat</ns0:orth>
        <ns0:pron>/biːt/</ns0:pron>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>v</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>apalear</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>aporracear</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>golpear [repetidamente]</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>paporrear</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>percutar</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>percutir</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
      </ns0:sense>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>latir</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>(intransitive) To move with pulsation or throbbing.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>batir</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>golpear</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>vencer</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>derrotar</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>pegar</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>apalizar</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>(transitive) To win against; to defeat or overcome; to do or be better than (someone); to excel in a particular, competitive event.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>batir</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>revolver</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>sacudir</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>To mix food in a rapid fashion. Compare whip.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>To exercise severely; to perplex; to trouble.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>beat around the bush</ns0:orth>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>v</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>andarse con rodeos</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>andar con ambages</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>(idiomatic) To treat a topic, but omit its main points, often intentionally.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>andarse por las ramas</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>ir por los cerros de Úbeda</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>(idiomatic) To delay or avoid talking about something difficult or unpleasant.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>beat it</ns0:orth>
        <ns0:pron>/ˈbiˌdɪt/</ns0:pron>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>v</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>pirarse</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>largarse</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>pirárselas</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>(idiomatic, chiefly, as imperative, pejorative, colloquial, dismissal) To leave; to go away.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>beat someone at their own game</ns0:orth>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>v</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>vencerlo en su propio juego</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>beat the system</ns0:orth>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>v</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>vencer al sistema</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>beat to</ns0:orth>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>v</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>adelantar</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>adelantarse</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>anticiparse</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>atrasar</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>ganar la delantera</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>beat to a pulp</ns0:orth>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>v</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>caerle la del pulpo</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>(transitive) To beat up (a person) more than usually severely.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>hacer fosfatina</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>hacer papilla</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>hacer puré</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>(transitive, colloquial, loosely) To defeat severely in various, even non-contact, competitive sports.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>beat to the punch</ns0:orth>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>v</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>adelantarse</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>anticipar</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>atrasar</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>ganar de mano</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>ganar por la mano</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>(idiomatic, transitive) To carry out an action before another person is able to do so.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>beat up</ns0:orth>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>v</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>zurrar</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>apalear</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>aporracear</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>aporrear</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>caerle golpe</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>coñacear</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>(transitive) To give a severe beating to; to assault violently with repeated blows.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>martirizar</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>preocuparse</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>(reflexive) To feel badly guilty and accuse (oneself) over something. (Usually followed by over or about.)</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>beatbox</ns0:orth>
        <ns0:pron>/ˈbiːt.bɑks/</ns0:pron>
        <ns0:pron>/ˈbiːʔ.bɑks/</ns0:pron>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>n</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>beatbox</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>(music) A type of electronic percussion device.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>beatboxing</ns0:orth>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>n</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>beatboxing</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>beater</ns0:orth>
        <ns0:pron>/ˈbitɚ/</ns0:pron>
        <ns0:pron>/ˈbiːtə/</ns0:pron>
        <ns0:pron>[ˈbiɾɚ]</ns0:pron>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>n</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>batidor</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>batidora</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>A kitchen implement for mixing.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>montero</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>batidor</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>A person who drives game towards shooters in a hunting party, typically working in a group with other beaters.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>beatific vision</ns0:orth>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>n</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>visión beatífica</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>(Christianity, theology) The eternal and direct visual perception of God.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>beatification</ns0:orth>
        <ns0:pron>/biˌætɪfɪˈkeɪʃən/</ns0:pron>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>n</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>beatificación</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>The act of beatifying, or the state of being beatified; especially, in the Roman Catholic Church, the act or process of ascertaining and declaring that a deceased person is one of "the blessed," or has attained the second degree of sanctity, — usually a stage in the process of canonization.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>beatify</ns0:orth>
        <ns0:pron>/biˈætɪfaɪ/</ns0:pron>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>v</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>beatificar</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>(transitive, Roman Catholicism) To carry out the third of four steps in canonization, making someone a blessed.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>beating</ns0:orth>
        <ns0:pron>/ˈbiːtɪŋ/</ns0:pron>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>n</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>paliza</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>A heavy defeat or setback.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>paliza</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>latido</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>golpiza</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>The pulsation of the heart.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>beatnik</ns0:orth>
        <ns0:pron>/ˈbiːtnɪk/</ns0:pron>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>n</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>beatnik</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>A person associated with the Beat Generation of the 1950s and 1960s or its style.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>beautician</ns0:orth>
        <ns0:pron>/bjuːˈtɪ(t)ʃən/</ns0:pron>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>n</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>esteticista</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>beautification</ns0:orth>
        <ns0:pron>/bjuːtɪfɪˈkeɪʃən/</ns0:pron>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>n</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>embellecimiento</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>Making beautiful, beautifying, improving the appearance of something.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>beautiful</ns0:orth>
        <ns0:pron>/ˈbju.tɪ.fəl/</ns0:pron>
        <ns0:pron>/ˈbjuːtɪ.fəl/</ns0:pron>
        <ns0:pron>/ˈbjuːtɪ.fʊl/</ns0:pron>
        <ns0:pron>[bju.ɾə.fəl]</ns0:pron>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>adj</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>bonito</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>bello</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>hermoso</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>lindo</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>guapo</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>bel</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>Possessing beauty, impressing the eye; attractive. [from 1520s]</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>bueno</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>alegre</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>bravo</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>despejado</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>Affording pleasure to any of the senses, especially that of hearing; delightful. [from 1860s]</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>bravo</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>Impressing with charm in an intellectual or moral way, through inherent suitability or elegance. [from 1580s]</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>beautifully</ns0:orth>
        <ns0:pron>/ˈbjuːtɪf(ə)li/</ns0:pron>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>adv</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>bellamente</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>In a beautiful manner.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>beautifulness</ns0:orth>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>n</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>belleza</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>The quality of being beautiful; beauty.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>beautify</ns0:orth>
        <ns0:pron>/ˈbjuː.tɪ.faɪ/</ns0:pron>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>v</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>embellecer</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>enchular</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>hermosear</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>(transitive) To make beautiful; to increase the beauty of.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>beauty</ns0:orth>
        <ns0:pron>/ˈbjuti/</ns0:pron>
        <ns0:pron>/ˈbjuːti/</ns0:pron>
        <ns0:pron>/ˈbuːti/</ns0:pron>
        <ns0:pron>[-ɾi]</ns0:pron>
        <ns0:pron>[ˈb(j)ɪu̯ɾ̥ɪ]</ns0:pron>
        <ns0:pron>[ˈbju̟ti]</ns0:pron>
        <ns0:pron>[ˈbju̟ːɾi]</ns0:pron>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>n</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>belleza</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>hermosura</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>beldad</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>fermosura</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>lindeza</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>preciosidad</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>(uncountable) The quality of being (especially visually) attractive, pleasing, fine or good-looking; comeliness.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>belleza</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>guapa</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>guapo</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>Someone who is beautiful.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>(in the plural) Those aspects or elements that make someone or something beautiful.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>belleza</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>hermosura</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>Something that is particularly good or pleasing.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>beauty is in the eye of the beholder</ns0:orth>
        <ns0:pron>/ˈbjuːti ɪz ɪn ðiː aɪ əv ðiː bɪˈhəʊldə/</ns0:pron>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>proverb</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>la belleza está en los ojos del mirante</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>la belleza está en los ojos del observador</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>la belleza está en los ojos del que la mira</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>Different people have different views on what is beautiful; beauty is subjective.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>beauty pageant</ns0:orth>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>n</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>concurso de belleza</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>A competition in which participants compete for a determination that one is the most physically attractive.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>beauty parlor</ns0:orth>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>n</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>salón de belleza</ns0:quote>
          <ns0:quote>salón de estética</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>(US, Philippines) A salon where hairdressers, beauticians, and cosmeticians work.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>beauty spot</ns0:orth>
        <ns0:pron>/ˈbjuti ˌspɑt/</ns0:pron>
        <ns0:pron>/ˈbjuːtɪ ˌspɒt/</ns0:pron>
        <ns0:pron>[-ɾi-]</ns0:pron>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>n</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>lunar</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>A natural mark on a person's skin, especially a freckle or mole on a woman's face.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>beaver</ns0:orth>
        <ns0:pron>/ˈbivɚ/</ns0:pron>
        <ns0:pron>/ˈbiːvə/</ns0:pron>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>n</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>castor</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>(countable) A semiaquatic rodent of the genus Castor, having a wide, flat tail and webbed feet, native to the Northern Hemisphere.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>chocho</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>(chiefly, North American, slang, countable) The pubic hair near a vulva or a vulva itself; (attributively) denoting films or literature featuring nude women.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
      <ns0:form>
        <ns0:orth>bec de corbin</ns0:orth>
      </ns0:form>
      <ns0:gramGrp>
        <ns0:pos>n</ns0:pos>
      </ns0:gramGrp>
      <ns0:sense>
        <ns0:cit type="trans" xml:lang="es">
          <ns0:quote>bec de corbin</ns0:quote>
        </ns0:cit>
        <ns0:sense>
          <ns0:def>(weaponry, historical) A poleaxe with a modified hammerhead and a spike mounted on the top of the pole.</ns0:def>
        </ns0:sense>
      </ns0:sense>
    </ns0:entry>
    <ns0:entry xmlns:ns0="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
